WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:04.240
Add fifty-eight and sixty-seven, and explain what each

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:05.470
carry really means.

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:12.850
In the units column, eight plus seven is fifteen units.

00:00:13.520 --> 00:00:15.290
Ten of those units make one ten.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:17.240
Carry that ten to the next column,

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:19.010
and five units remain.

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:23.020
In the tens column there are five tens, six tens,

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:25.080
and the carried ten: twelve tens.

00:00:25.510 --> 00:00:27.040
Ten of those tens make one hundred.

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:29.860
Carry it, and two tens remain.

00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:34.020
The answer is one hundred, two tens and five units:

00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:35.460
one hundred and twenty-five.

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:38.720
Neither starting number has a hundreds digit.

00:00:39.390 --> 00:00:42.470
The hundreds digit in the answer exists only because of

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:43.420
the second carry.

00:00:44.270 --> 00:00:45.140
Check two ways.

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:48.060
Roughly, sixty plus seventy is one hundred and thirty,

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:49.680
which is close.

00:00:50.630 --> 00:00:53.080
Exactly, fifty plus sixty is one hundred and ten,

00:00:54.030 --> 00:00:56.986
eight plus seven is fifteen, and together they make one

00:00:56.986 --> 00:00:57.420
hundred and twenty-five.

00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:02.190
A carry is ten of one place traded for one of

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:02.980
the next place.

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:06.730
Rebuild this explanation, then add seventy-six and

00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:09.360
eighty-nine, saying what each carry means.
